    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 62 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`, including the new `Cp50Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent create-owner support for `POST /api/owners`. When a request carries an `Idempotency-Key` header that was already used to create an owner, the endpoint now returns the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (or 409-ing on the duplicate-identity check).\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions, I added:\n\n**Pipeline steps** (`rest/function/owner/`)\n- `CheckIdempotencyKey` \u2014 new first step. Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header via `ServerHttpConnection`. If the key was seen before, it throws a checked `IdempotentReplayException(ownerId)` to short-circuit the pipeline; otherwise it publishes the key as an `Out<IdempotencyKey>` variable.\n- `RecordIdempotencyKey` \u2014 new step after `save`. Records the key against the persisted owner id (no-op when no header was sent).\n- `IdempotencyKey` \u2014 a small record holder for the variable.\n\n**Shared bean** (`rest/function/common/`)\n- `IdempotencyStore` \u2014 a `@Component` `ConcurrentMap<String, Integer>` (key \u2192 owner id), injected by type.\n\n**Escalation** (`rest/escalation/`)\n- `IdempotentReplayException` + `IdempotentReplayExceptionHandler` \u2014 the handler loads the original owner and responds `200` with its `OwnerDto`.\n- Registered via `escalation/\u2026IdempotentReplayException.yml`.\n\n**Wiring** (`owners.POST.yml`)\n- Inserted `checkIdempotency` as the entry point (before `validate`) and `recordIdempotency` right after `save`.\n\nDesign notes: the check runs *before* validation/insert so a replay never re-validates or re-inserts; recording happens *after* save so the generated id exists and only a successful create is remembered. `Owner.pets` is `EAGER`, so mapping the replayed owner in the escalation handler needs no open session.",
