    "probe_text": "I now have the full picture. Here is the complete, ordered account of what happens on `POST /api/owners`, read from the current YAML pipeline (`owners.POST.yml`) and every function class it wires together.\n\n## Endpoint guard (before the pipeline runs)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. A caller lacking that role is rejected (`AuthorizationDeniedException` handler) before any step executes.\n\n## Pipeline steps, in execution order\n\n**1. `CheckIdempotencyKey`** (no transaction)\n- Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` request header.\n- *Validation/short-circuit:* if that key was already used, throws `IdempotentReplayException` \u2192 the original owner is replayed with **200** and nothing below runs.\n- *Side effect:* publishes an `IdempotencyKey` variable (holding the key, or `null` if the header is absent) for later recording.\n\n**2. `ValidateOwnerFields`** (no transaction) \u2014 binds the request body once and runs all field validation/normalization. Any accumulated failures throw `OwnerFieldsValidationException` \u2192 **400** with an `errors` array naming each bad field. In order within the step:\n- *Validation:* `firstName` required (non-blank).\n- *Validation:* `lastName` required.\n- *Validation + side effect (address):* normalizes address \u2014 prefers structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`) and composes them into `address`; else normalizes the flat `address`; if neither is present, adds an `address` error. Mutates the request in place.\n- *Validation:* `city` required.\n- *Validation:* `telephone` required.\n- *Validation + side effect (telephone):* normalizes telephone to E.164 (keeps a leading `+`/country code, else assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0`; strips spaces/dashes/brackets; 8\u201315 total digits; national-length rule: `+61`\u21929 digits, `+1`\u219210). Invalid \u2192 `telephone` error. Mutates the request.\n- *Validation + side effect (email, optional):* if present, must be syntactically valid **and** its domain must not be on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`); invalid/blocked \u2192 `email` error. When valid, lower-cases and stores it back. Absent/blank is accepted.\n- *Validation (postcode, optional):* if present, must be exactly 4 digits; and for a city with a known region it must fall in range (Sydney/NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne/VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane/QLD 4000\u20134099). Out of range/malformed \u2192 `postcode` error.\n- *Validation (registrationDate, optional):* if present, must not be after the server's current date (no future dating) \u2192 `registrationDate` error.\n- *Side effect:* republishes the validated/normalized DTO for later steps.\n\n> The write transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]`) begins at the next step and spans everything through the response, so all the following duplicate/count checks read within the same transaction as the insert.\n\n**3. `CheckIdentityUnique`** \u2014 *Validation.* Scans all non-soft-deleted owners; rejects with `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 **409** if an existing owner has the **same normalized telephone AND the same (case-insensitive) email**. (Two same-household owners with different phones do *not* collide.)\n\n**4. `CheckHouseholdUnique`** \u2014 *Validation.* Skipped if the request set `sharesHousehold`, or if postcode is missing. Otherwise computes `householdId` (from normalized lastName + postcode) and rejects with `DuplicateHouseholdException` \u2192 **409** if any non-deleted owner already has that `householdId`.\n\n**5. `CheckCityCapacity`** \u2014 *Validation.* Counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); rejects with `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409** if the count is **\u2265 50**.\n\n**6. `BuildOwner`** \u2014 *Side effect.* Maps the validated DTO into a new `Owner` entity (via `OwnerMapper`).\n\n**7. `DefaultRegistrationDate`** \u2014 *Side effect.* Resolves the registration date (supplied value, else today) and rolls it forward off weekends and listed 2026 public holidays to the next business day. Mutates the entity in place.\n\n**8. `CheckDailyLimit`** \u2014 *Validation.* Counts owners already registered on that adjusted date; rejects with `DailyLimitExceededException` \u2192 **429** if the count is **\u2265 100**.\n\n**9. `AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 *Side effect.* Assigns `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode\u2192city\u2192`UNKNOWN`; HASH8 = first 8 upper hex of SHA-256 of `telephone+lastName`), appending `-<n>` (smallest `n \u2265 2`) on collision with an existing code.\n\n**10. `AssignHouseholdId`** \u2014 *Side effect.* Sets `householdId` = first 12 upper hex of SHA-256 of `normalizedLastName|postcode`.\n\n**11. `AssignHouseholdMemberCount`** \u2014 *Side effect.* Sets `householdMemberCount` = existing owners sharing that `householdId` **+ 1** (this new owner).\n\n**12. `AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 *Side effect.* Sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing firstName + lastName (case-insensitive), excluding this one.\n\n**13. `AssignBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 *Side effect.* Sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` when **> 80** owners were already registered on the adjusted date.\n\n**14. `AssignPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 *Side effect.* Sets `possibleDuplicate = false` by default; unless `sharesHousehold`, flags `possibleDuplicate = true` with `possibleDuplicateOf = <matching owner id>` when a non-deleted owner shares lastName (case-insensitive) + postcode but has a **different** telephone.\n\n**15. `SaveOwner`** \u2014 *Side effect.* Persists the owner (`ownerRepository.save`), assigning its id.\n\n**16. `RecordIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 *Side effect.* Records the `Idempotency-Key` \u2192 new owner id in the `IdempotencyStore` (no-op if no key was supplied), enabling later replay.\n\n**17. `AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *Side effect.* Emits an `AUDIT` log line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel and membershipNumber.\n\n**18. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *Side effect.* Maps the entity to `OwnerDto` and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`. The transaction commits once here at the end.\n\n---\n\nA couple of things worth flagging, since they diverge from the inline comments:\n- The `owners.POST.yml` comment claims `checkIdentityUnique` \"consolidates the former separate telephone, email and household checks\" and that the check is on the \"WHOLE derived identityKey.\" The actual `CheckIdentityUnique` code only compares **telephone + email** (it never compares `householdId`); the household dimension is enforced separately by step 4. So the comment overstates what that one step does.\n- `CheckCityCapacity`, `CheckDailyLimit`, `AssignHouseholdMemberCount`, `AssignNamesakeCount`, and `AssignBulkSignupWarning` count **all** owners (they do not skip soft-deleted ones), whereas the identity/household/possible-duplicate checks explicitly ignore `deleted` owners \u2014 an inconsistency in how \"existing owners\" is defined across the pipeline."
